                <pb facs="0140" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg98"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Copy of a telegram from the collector of customs at
                        Liverpool to F. Goulburn, esq.</hi></head>
                <p>Georgiana, British, 407 tons register; brig rig; cargo, merchandise, provisions,
                    and drugs; no guns on deck; no fitting for guns on board; 1 cwt. powder; iron
                    bulwarks; no port-holes for guns; no fittings for guns on board; a fast vessel;
                    40 crew; not fitted as a privateer; better adapted for running the blockade;
                    cleared out for Nassau; now in the Mersey, and is intended to leave to-day, say
                    4 p.m.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sunday</hi>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 18</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
